cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Legato or the Legato Office Bench, please cite it."
title: "Legato: an open-source computer-use harness"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Legato Labs"
repository-code: "https://github.com/legatolabs/legato"
url: "https://legato.computer"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - computer use
  - GUI agents
  - desktop automation
  - MCP
  - OSWorld
  - reinforcement learning
abstract: >-
  Legato drives a desktop for any OpenAI-compatible vision model: your own computer, a desktop container, any sandbox,
  or a cloud desktop. It waits for the screen to settle instead of sleeping, batches actions, keeps the prompt cache
  warm and bounds every model call. With the same Claude model on 24 office tasks it was 1.48x faster than Anthropic's
  reference loop at the same success rate.
